    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 151148\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n448 AM PDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the \n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Monday.\n\nTightened pressure gradients across the region will continue to \nbring gusty south-southwesterly winds to the forecast area in the \nafternoons thanks to an upper-level trough across the Pacific \nNorthwest and a ridge to our east. Expect gust speeds generally \nbetween 25 and 35 mph, though can't rule out 40 mph speeds in \nisolated instances and/or in the higher terrain. Ensembles \ncontinue to show a reinforcing closed low riding along the \nCalifornia Coast before pushing into the southern Great Basin mid-\nto-late week. The resultant instability coupled with 0.75 to 1.25\ninches of PWAT over our eastern zones have resulted in increased \nPoPs across southeastern Lincoln and northern and eastern Mohave \ncounties Wednesday and Thursday. Additionally, WPC has painted a \nMarginal Excessive Rainfall Outlook over northern Mohave County \nfor Wednesday and Thursday. Coverage is expected to be isolated, \nbut storms that form have the potential to be efficient rain- \nmakers. For locations west of Interstate 15, expect mostly dry \nconditions and temperatures near-normal heading into the next work\nweek.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light\nwinds early this morning will shift to the southeast, with gusts \nto 15-20KT developing by mid-morning. By early afternoon, winds \nveer to the south-southwest, increasing with gusts to 20-25KT \nexpected through sunset before diminishing. Winds become lighter \novernight, following similar trends heading into Wednesday \nmorning. VFR conditions prevail with no operationally significant\ncloud cover, and temperatures expected to top out at 99 degrees \nthis afternoon.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Winds around 5-10KT at  \nissuance will shift to the south and southeast, with gusts to \n15-20kt developing by mid morning, increasing to 20-25KT this\nafternoon through sunset. Winds become lighter overnight for \nmost, though intermittent gusts are expected through the night for\nportions of the Lower Colorado River Valley near KIFP. Primary \nexceptions are the northern Owens Valley/KBIH where gusty up- \nvalley winds expected this afternoon, and the western Mohave \nDesert/KDAG where west winds become gusty late afternoon through \nlate evening. Isolated thunderstorms are expected, mainly over\nnorthwestern Arizona and eastern Lincoln County this afternoon \nand evening, but otherwise, VFR conditions prevail with no \noperationally significant cloud cover elsewhere.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Soulat \nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
